{"name":"Pine Bark","hex":"#887468","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any coniferous tree of the genus Pinus.","Any tree (usually coniferous) which resembles a member of this genus in some respect."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A painful longing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pine"},{"term":"bark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a short, loud, explosive noise with the vocal organs (said of animals, especially dogs).","To make a clamor; to make importunate outcries."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The short, loud, explosive sound uttered by a dog, a fox, and some other animals.","An abrupt loud vocal utterance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bark"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bark (botany)","blocks":[{"text":"Bark is the outermost layer of stems and roots of woody plants. Plants with bark include trees, woody vines, and shrubs. Bark refers to all the tissues outside the vascular cambium and is a nontechnical term. It overlays the wood and consists of the inner bark and the outer bark. The inner bark, which in older stems is living tissue, includes the innermost layer of the periderm. The outer bark on older stems includes the dead tissue on the surface of the stems, along with parts of the outermost periderm and all the tissues on the outer side of the periderm. The outer bark on trees which lies external to the living periderm is also called the rhytidome."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/%E9%BB%91%E6%9D%BE_Pinus_thunbergii_20211007185113_01.jpg/330px-%E9%BB%91%E6%9D%BE_Pinus_thunbergii_20211007185113_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bark_(botany)","wikidata":"Q184453"},{"title":"Pine","blocks":[{"text":"Pines ) are a genus of conifers in the family Pinaceae. Pinus is the sole genus in the subfamily Pinoideae. The species are trees or shrubs with their leaves in bunches, usually of 2 to 5 needles. The seeds are carried on woody cones, with two seeds to each cone scale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Pinus_jeffreyi_at_Lassen_Volcanic_National_Park.jpg/330px-Pinus_jeffreyi_at_Lassen_Volcanic_National_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pine","wikidata":"Q12024"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Poskozena_borka_na_tresni_20210821_150436.jpg/500px-Poskozena_borka_na_tresni_20210821_150436.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Poskozena_borka_na_tresni_20210821_150436.jpg/1280px-Poskozena_borka_na_tresni_20210821_150436.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Poskozena_borka_na_tresni_20210821_150436.jpg/500px-Poskozena_borka_na_tresni_20210821_150436.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Damaged bark of a cherry tree","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APoskozena_borka_na_tresni_20210821_150436.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/BarkAndWire-0308.jpg/500px-BarkAndWire-0308.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/BarkAndWire-0308.jpg/1280px-BarkAndWire-0308.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/BarkAndWire-0308.jpg/500px-BarkAndWire-0308.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Living tree bark enveloping barbed wire","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarkAndWire-0308.jpg"},{"srcset":"https:/